# --- Deny-by-default credential exclusion ---
#
# THIS FILE IS THE SECURITY BOUNDARY, not chezmoi's `private_` attribute.
#
# `private_` cannot be relied on. It is a documented no-op on Windows
# (internal/chezmoi/realsystem_windows.go: `Chmod` returns nil), it is
# silently ignored when the prefix order is wrong (`dot_private_x` applies
# as `~/.private_x` mode 0644, exit 0), and `encrypted_` does not imply it.
# `chezmoi doctor` reports "no suspicious entries" in all three cases.
#
# TWO PATTERN RULES, both verified, both counter-intuitive:
#
#   1. NEVER exclude a credential directory by its directory form. Writing
#      `.ssh/` makes re-inclusion IMPOSSIBLE, because git never descends
#      into an excluded directory. Glob the CONTENTS: `**/.ssh/*`.
#   2. A pattern containing `/` is ANCHORED. `.ssh/*` does not match
#      `sub/.ssh/id_rsa`. Prefix with `**/` for any depth.
#
# A pattern here has no effect on a path git ALREADY tracks. Audit with
# `git ls-files` before trusting this file.

# --- credential directories: glob contents, never the directory ---
**/.ssh/*
**/.gnupg/*
**/.aws/*
**/.azure/*
**/.config/gcloud/*
**/.kube/*
**/.docker/*
**/.config/gh/*
**/.config/hub

# --- key material by shape, unanchored so it matches at any depth ---
id_*
*_rsa
*_dsa
*_ecdsa
*_ed25519
*_ecdsa_sk
*_ed25519_sk
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
*.ppk
*.asc
*.gpg
*.kdbx

# --- token and credential files ---
.netrc
_netrc
.npmrc
.pypirc
.env
.env.*
*.env
credentials
credentials.*
*.credentials
*_token
*.token

# --- shell and tool history (routinely captures secrets typed inline) ---
*_history
.viminfo
.lesshst

# --- editor and OS noise ---
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json

# --- generated by the link checker and test runners ---
lychee.md
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/

# --- bootstrap backups: never commit a snapshot of a real machine ---
.dotfiles-backup-*/
*.dotfiles-backup.tar.gz

# --- narrow re-includes: the ONLY things allowed back ---
# Public keys are public by construction. `~/.ssh/config` and
# `allowed_signers` are the intended payload. Everything else stays out.
!**/.ssh/config
!**/.ssh/allowed_signers
!.env.example
